# The reviewed-algorithm anchor byte-compares every POLICY_CODE_REPO_PATHS
# entry against its committed Git blob.  Git for Windows sets
# core.autocrlf=true by default, which checks these files out with CRLF while
# the blobs hold LF, so the anchor refuses on the supported platform and the
# reviewed-authority path becomes unreachable.  Store and check out exact
# bytes instead of normalizing them.
#
# This also protects the blobs: with translation on, a later `git add` of a
# CRLF working copy would rewrite the policy bytes and invalidate the frozen
# candidate's policy_code_sha256 map.
* -text
